<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Usiminas first half up.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Usiminas first half up.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private Brazilian steelmaker Usiminas on Monday reported the following first-half 1997 financial results.</p>
<p>		     Jan-June 1997	   Jan-June 1996</p>
<p>Net		  152.1 million	   114.2 million</p>
<p>Shr Net	    0.6818 real	     0.5119 real</p>
<p>Gross Profit     262 million	     190.5 million</p>
<p>Oper Profit	202.9 million	   159.4 million</p>
<p>Pre-tax Profit   221.8 million	   159.2 million</p>
<p>Net Sales	  892.9 million	   759.98 million</p>
<p>Net Worth	3.003 billion	   2.843 billion</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in Brazilian reais and are not adjusted for inflation.</p>
<p>The company also said in a statement that net profit adjusted for inflation reached 152.3 million reais, or 0.6825 real per share.</p>
<p>((-- James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413))</p>
